‹Heading1,b:Review drawer›
‹Rule:────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────›

‹Code: leader d › slides a ‹Text,b:review drawer› in from the right over half the body and shows the focused pane's
diff: an agent's ‹Text,i:last turn›, or its branch against the base. See the ‹Link,u:design notes› for the keys; it
replaces ‹Text,s:the old layout pane›. Press ‹Key,b:esc› to hand the keyboard back.

‹AlertNote:▎ ›‹AlertNote,b:󰋽 Note›
‹AlertNote:▎ ›The panes under the drawer keep their size, so no agent redraws when it opens or closes.

‹Heading2,b:What changed›

  ‹Bullet:• ›The ported tuios ‹Code: diffview › draws the lines, with highlighting from the theme
  ‹Bullet:• ›One watcher per worktree, shared by every agent in it
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›the turn gate skips unchanged snapshots
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›the agents rail re-probes on a branch switch
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›which fixes the stale ‹Code: main › on the cards
  ‹Bullet:• ›‹Code: leader n › picks a worktree for a new agent
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›‹Image:󰥶 The drawer in a list  ›‹ImageHost:github.com›
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›‹SummaryMark,b:▸ ›‹Summary,b:Keys in the list›‹FoldHint:   enter opens›

‹Heading3,b:Checklist›

  ‹TaskDone,b:✓ ›‹Code: make check ›‹TaskDoneText: passes›
  ‹TaskDone,b:✓ ›‹TaskDoneText:Goldens in Mocha and Latte›
  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›The macOS CI step for the watcher fix

‹Heading2,b:How to test›

  ‹Bullet:1. ›Open three agents in master-stack: ‹Code: leader n › three times
  ‹Bullet:2. ›Run a prompt in the master, then press ‹Code: leader d ›
  ‹Bullet:3. ›Step through the turns with ‹Code: , › and ‹Code: . ›

